try receive on an empty pipe: 0x80028223
try send that fills the pipe: 0x00000000
try send on a full pipe: 0x80028222
try receive that empties the pipe: 0x00000000
try receive on an unknown pipe: 0x80028221
try receive of zero bytes on an empty pipe: 0x00000000
try receive of zero bytes receives nothing: 0x00000000
try receive FULL of more than there is: 0x80028223
receive DONT_REMOVE: 0x00000000
receive DONT_REMOVE gets the data: 0x00000003
receive ASAP of more than there is: 0x00000000
receive ASAP gets what there is: 0x00000003
the data is still there after DONT_REMOVE: 0x00000001
receive ASAP removed it: 0x80028223
a waiting receive gets the data sent: 0x00000000
the data received is the data sent: 0x00000001
cancel: 0x00000000
cancel counts the waiting senders: 0x00000000
cancel counts the waiting receivers: 0x00000001
a canceled receive: 0x80028007
delete: 0x00000000
a receive on a deleted pipe: 0x80028006
DONE
